  - "**/*.js"
alwaysApply: false
---
# SECURITY
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt/argon (Laravel default). HTTP-only, SameSite cookies; session lifetime 120 min.
- CSRF on every state-changing form/AJAX call; server-side validation on all input; escape all output.
- File uploads: whitelist type (pdf, doc/docx, xls/xlsx, ppt/pptx, jpg/png/gif, txt), max 25MB, stored outside `public/`.
- Sensitive fields (PII/financial) encrypted at rest where flagged; secrets only in `.env`, never committed.
- Audit trail for create/update/delete/ownership change (who, what, when). Rate-limit login and API.
- Review each feature for: missing policy, mass assignment (`$fillable`), IDOR (record-level access), N+1, unvalidated input.

# PERFORMANCE
- Page < 3s, save < 2s, simple search < 1s, report < 5s (<10k rows). Index for tables > 100k rows; paginate; cache hot lookups.

# TESTING (PHPUnit / Pest with MySQL)
- Minimum 80% coverage of business logic. Each requirement ID has at least one feature test.
- Required tests per module: authorization by role, validation rules, happy path, edge cases (e.g. lead conversion,
  stage probability change, closed-case read-only, lockout after 5 attempts).
- Run `php artisan test` and `./vendor/bin/pint --test` before opening a PR; CI must be green to merge.
